#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054425 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33551349-bb39-5a79-bf56-a4df753201ed" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Elements of a Set"}] :question/id #uuid "16e0f524-49b5-549d-8e60-8597379c4350" :question/math-academy-id "e-13134" :question/problem "List the elements of the following set:\n$A = \\big\\{a, c,3, \\{c,3 \\}, \\emptyset, \\{\\emptyset\\}\\big\\}$" :question/worked-solution "The elements of the set $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\na, \\quad c, \\quad 3, \\quad \\{c,3\\}, \\quad \\emptyset, \\quad \\{\\emptyset\\}\n$$\n\n**Watch Out!**\n\n- The elements $c,3$, and $\\{c,3\\}$ are three separate entities. The first two are the elements $c$ and $3$, and the third is a set *containing* these two elements.\n- The elements $\\emptyset$ and $\\{\\emptyset \\}$ are also separate entities. The first one is the empty set (i.e., the set containing no elements), while the second is a set that contains the empty set."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054426 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054849 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de59db4d-82d5-5bad-a559-bf5396375355" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Non-Sets"}] :question/id #uuid "046f7284-3715-555c-bdc9-c108db061205" :question/math-academy-id "e-13135" :question/problem "Which of the following is **not** a set?\n\n1. $\\{2, 4, 6 \\}$\n2. $\\{\\{2 \\}, \\{4, 6 \\} \\}$\n3. $2, 4, 6$\n4. $\\emptyset$" :question/worked-solution "A set is a collection of elements listed between two braces (curly brackets). However, note that the null set (the set that does not contain any elements) can be written as either $\\{\\}$ or $\\emptyset$.\n\n- $\\{2, 4, 6 \\}$ is a set. The elements are $2$, $4$, and $6$, and they are listed between two braces.\n- $\\{\\{2 \\}, \\{4, 6 \\} \\}$ is a set. The elements are $\\{2 \\}$ and $\\{4, 6 \\}$, and are listed between the two outermost braces.\n- $2, 4, 6$ is *not* a set. The numbers $2$, $4$, and $6$ are *not* listed between two braces.\n- $\\emptyset$ is the empty set. Therefore, it is a set.\n\nIn conclusion, only III is not a set."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054427 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054850 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "900f0d3d-6a5c-53b2-b987-eee1a8963b6b" :knowledge-point/title "Using Element Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "5404d545-570b-53d7-b16a-b23a371d4abd" :question/math-academy-id "e-13136" :question/problem "Write the following statement using element notation:\n\n$\\qquad$ $1$ and $2$ are elements of a set $S$, but $3$, $4$, and $5$ are not." :question/worked-solution "If $a$ is an element of $S$, we write $a \\in S$. Otherwise, if $a$ is *not* an element of $S$, we write $a \\notin S$.\n\n- Since $1$ and $2$ are elements of $S$, we write $1,2 \\in S$.\n- Since $3$, $4$, and $5$ are *not* elements of $S$, we write $3,4,5 \\notin S$.\n\nAll together, we have the following statement:\n\n$$\n1,2 \\in S\\quad \\textrm{and}\\quad 3,4,5 \\notin S\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054428 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054851 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ceb6c84-a16b-5519-abd6-d2bb72ea81d3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Set Corresponding to a Description"}] :question/id #uuid "0684e366-bcf4-5b08-8eae-6600a88e2920" :question/math-academy-id "e-13137" :question/problem "Express the following sets using an ellipsis:\n\n- The set $X$ of all positive integers greater than or equal to $10$\n- The set $Y$ of integers less than zero\n- The set $A$ of all natural numbers greater than $5$ and less than $5\\, 005$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that an ellipsis means \"and so on up to\" if it's followed by a specific element, or \"and so on\" if not.\n\n- To express the set $X$, we start with the first positive integer greater than or equal to $10$, which is $10$. The next integer is $11$, the one after that is $12$, and so on, which we denote with an ellipsis:\n$X = \\{10, 11, 12, \\ldots \\}$\n- To express the set $Y$, we start with the first integer less than zero, which is $-1$. The next integer less than zero is $-2$, the one after that is $-3$, and so on, which we denote with an ellipsis:\n$Y = \\{-1, -2, -3, \\ldots \\}$\nHowever, note that it is conventional to write a set of numbers from least to greatest, just like is shown on the number line. Writing the elements of $Y$ from least to greatest, we have\n$Y = \\{\\ldots, -3, -2, -1\\}$.\n- To express the set $A$, we start with the first positive integer greater than $5$, which is $6$. The next integer is $7$, the one after that is $8$, and so on up to $5\\, 004$ (the largest integer less than $5\\, 005$). So, we have\n$A = \\{6, 7, 8, \\ldots, 5004\\}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054970 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33551349-bb39-5a79-bf56-a4df753201ed" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Elements of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5d15618-ae94-5ef1-a113-791e81794396" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{d}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051351} {:answer/id #uuid "04702cca-1fd2-51b1-9088-3795323ec74a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051352} {:answer/id #uuid "34d077d0-b217-5819-942e-7a3ca19d31ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051353} {:answer/id #uuid "605ca6b6-a3df-57e6-808c-7dd385c9eb3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051354} {:answer/id #uuid "6d231f10-902f-5c12-93a2-d50e881243f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051355}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e8aa0f78-c767-5f71-9f45-b378b603712a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051350}] :question/id #uuid "a7b3410f-37c1-59bb-9c9d-28bb9b75dbb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-1150" :question/problem "Which of the following is an element of the set $C = {{a}, b, {c}, d, {e}}$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054850 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "900f0d3d-6a5c-53b2-b987-eee1a8963b6b" :knowledge-point/title "Using Element Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f216052-b042-5650-b7c1-f56d813bb264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a, b, c ∉ S" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051363} {:answer/id #uuid "973501b7-20a2-561e-9cdb-a2e67572d6e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "d, e ∈ S" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051364} {:answer/id #uuid "b1434d4a-3e58-5dfd-8acb-d5d13c5bb75e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a, b, c ∉ S$ and $d, e ∈ S$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051365} {:answer/id #uuid "cf72a39d-e96c-59f7-b87e-82bf7b8787d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a, b ∈ S$ and $c, d, e ∉ S$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051366} {:answer/id #uuid "fb8f170e-df2c-5a3b-bfe7-914ce60157f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a, b, c ∈ S$ and $d, e ∉ S$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051367}] :answer-field/id #uuid "bbeb8dbc-dca5-5d86-981e-fbd5f85769d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186051362}] :question/id #uuid "126eb637-e5ca-5143-b535-559e40bc4ac8" :question/math-academy-id "q-1166" :question/problem "If $a, b$, and $c$ are elements of $S$, but $d$ and $e$ are not, then which of the following is true?"}]}
